<title>UK: UK M4 grows provisional 9.8 pct in year to Sept.</title>
<headline>UK M4 grows provisional 9.8 pct in year to Sept.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England published the following data on UK monetary aggregates for September -</p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY				     SEPT	 AUGUST*</p>
<p>     M4 in month	  (adjusted)	     +0.8	  +1.0</p>
<p>	  in year to date (adjusted)	     +9.8	  +9.5</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (unadjusted)	    +0.7	  +0.9</p>
<p>	  in year to date (unadjusted)	   +9.8	  +9.5</p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks, building</p>
<p>     societies in billions of stg		 3.5	   5.4</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecasts M4 9.6 pct yr/yr, M4 lending +5.3 billion stg. * Previously published final figures for M4  </p>
<p>    Three-month annual M4 rate (adj)	   +9.4	  +8.4#</p>
<p>    Six-month annual M4 rate   (adj)	   +8.9	  +9.4#</p>
<p># Previous figures from provisional August M4 release</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
